A majestic ancient oak tree with an intricate root system visible beneath the soil surface, rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive swirling brushstroke style. The roots mirror the branches above in complexity and spread, creating a symmetrical balance between underground and canopy. The soil layer reveals interconnected root networks glowing with warm amber and ochre tones, while the crown above bursts with vibrant emerald and teal leaves painted in thick, expressive impasto strokes. The swirling sky features Van Gogh's signature spiraling clouds in deep blues and purples. Small birds nest in the branches while beneficial insects traverse the roots below. The entire composition emphasizes organic growth, interconnection, and the hidden foundations that support visible flourishing. Golden hour lighting casts long shadows and creates a sense of vitality and timeless wisdom.
